## Core Data Models

### Task
The central entity representing a work item on the kanban board.

```go
type Task struct {
    ID           uint           // Primary key
    UserID       uint           // Owner
    Title        string         // Task name
    Project      string         // Project name (string, not FK)
    Duration     int            // Total duration in seconds (calculated from sessions)
    SessionCount int            // Number of work sessions
    Tags         []string       // Array of tag strings
    ColumnIndex  int            // Kanban column (0=first, 1=second, etc.)
    Status       string         // "uncompleted" or "completed"
    Position     int            // Order within column
    IsActive     bool           // Timer currently running
    Sessions     []Session      // Related work sessions
}
```

### Session
Represents a work interval on a task. **Sessions are the single source of truth for duration.**

```go
type Session struct {
    ID         uint       // Primary key
    TaskID     uint       // Parent task
    StartTime  time.Time  // When session started
    EndTime    *time.Time // When ended (nil if active)
    Duration   int        // Duration in seconds
    SessionNum int        // Sequential number (1, 2, 3...)
}
```

### UserColumn
User-defined kanban columns (customizable names).

```go
type UserColumn struct {
    ID       uint   // Primary key
    UserID   uint   // Owner
    Project  string // Optional project scope
    ColIndex int    // Column position (0, 1, 2...)
    Name     string // Display name ("Todo", "In Progress", etc.)
}
```

### User
Authentication and preferences.

```go
type User struct {
    ID           uint     // Primary key
    Email        string   // Unique, login identifier
    Name         string   // Display name
    PasswordHash string   // bcrypt hash
    Role         string   // "user" or "admin"
    Plan         string   // "normal", "pro", "vip"
    Actionbar    []string // UI preference for action bar buttons
}
```

